1
00:00:36,637 --> 00:00:40,257
<i>Ours was a love story like no other.</i>

2
00:00:40,258 --> 00:00:44,061
<i>It's like a film written by Ricky Lee.</i>

3
00:00:44,916 --> 00:00:49,654
<i>But in our version,
she's no damsel in distress.</i>

4
00:00:49,654 --> 00:00:51,622
<i>She needed no saving.</i>

5
00:00:51,622 --> 00:00:56,860
<i>As a matter of fact,
I was the one who needed to be saved.</i>

6
00:01:06,518 --> 00:01:10,408
Mister! Help! Help!

7
00:01:10,408 --> 00:01:12,776
There's a giant crocodile!

8
00:01:17,982 --> 00:01:20,585
Sorry, Mister. I'm going to an audition.

9
00:01:20,585 --> 00:01:22,386
Sorry.

10
00:01:26,457 --> 00:01:29,927
<i>This is not the first time I've seen her.</i>

11
00:01:29,927 --> 00:01:32,095
I've known her for a long time.

12
00:01:32,697 --> 00:01:35,433
She was my classmate in college.

13
00:01:35,433 --> 00:01:39,137
If there's one thing permanent in our lives,

14
00:01:39,137 --> 00:01:40,738
it's change.

15
00:01:40,738 --> 00:01:43,408
Everything changes.

16
00:01:43,408 --> 00:01:46,310
You can change everything.

17
00:01:46,310 --> 00:01:48,593
That's the nature of reality,

18
00:01:48,593 --> 00:01:53,456
according to our Greek philosopher Heraclitus.

19
00:01:53,456 --> 00:01:57,989
Professor, I think...
I think my father would disagree.

20
00:01:57,989 --> 00:02:00,224
Why is that, Miss Trinidad?

21
00:02:04,055 --> 00:02:11,302
Because for him,
a lot of things are permanent in our lives.

22
00:02:11,302 --> 00:02:15,973
Like death, taxes...

23
00:02:17,557 --> 00:02:20,199
including his fear of my mom.

24
00:02:27,933 --> 00:02:30,013
<i>She was popular in college.</i>

25
00:02:31,285 --> 00:02:32,400
<i>I'm not sure if she knew me.</i>

26
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:34,339
<i>All I know is...</i>

27
00:02:36,490 --> 00:02:42,293
<i>my world becomes brighter whenever I see her.</i>

28
00:02:46,299 --> 00:02:50,771
<i>Why I didn't introduce myself to her...</i>

29
00:02:50,773 --> 00:02:53,132
<i>Why I did not approach her...</i>

30
00:02:53,132 --> 00:02:55,801
<i>Why I did not befriend her...</i>

31
00:02:58,631 --> 00:03:02,599
<i>Why I didn't try to court her.</i>

32
00:03:05,585 --> 00:03:11,257
<i>Let's just say
I'm waiting for the right time and opportunity</i>

33
00:03:11,258 --> 00:03:13,459
<i>to approach her.</i>

34
00:03:17,531 --> 00:03:21,701
<i>Unfortunately, I ran out of time.</i>

35
00:03:31,845 --> 00:03:34,714
<i>That was the last time I saw her.</i>

36
00:03:35,798 --> 00:03:37,869
<i>The next semester,</i>

37
00:03:37,871 --> 00:03:42,033
<i>we heard she dropped out of the university.</i>

38
00:03:42,033 --> 00:03:46,178
<i>And no one could tell
what had happened to her.</i>

39
00:03:51,734 --> 00:03:56,339
<i>I was like Ely Buendia
the next time I saw her.</i>

40
00:03:56,339 --> 00:04:01,544
<i>The same way he saw
his kind of ugly friend in a magazine.</i>

41
00:04:01,544 --> 00:04:04,574
<i>She was wearing yellow,
and her hair was green.</i>

42
00:04:04,574 --> 00:04:08,778
<i>But unlike in the song, I didn't judge her.</i>

43
00:04:08,778 --> 00:04:12,702
<i>Instead, I felt pride.</i>

44
00:04:12,702 --> 00:04:15,198
<i>Because the world deserves to know</i>

45
00:04:15,198 --> 00:04:18,821
<i>the most beautiful woman I've ever seen.</i>

46
00:04:18,821 --> 00:04:24,460
<i>The woman
who can make my heart beat fast and slow.</i>

47
00:04:25,962 --> 00:04:27,700
<i>Is this fate?</i>

48
00:04:27,701 --> 00:04:30,670
<i>Or is it divine providence?</i>

49
00:04:30,670 --> 00:04:35,442
<i>Imagine, after a long time, here she is.</i>

50
00:04:35,442 --> 00:04:38,078
<i>We are on the same trip.</i>

51
00:04:38,078 --> 00:04:42,816
<i>This is supposed
to be an escape from the city.</i>

52
00:04:42,816 --> 00:04:44,517
<i>But here I am,</i>

53
00:04:44,517 --> 00:04:48,888
<i>facing the feelings
I've long been trying to escape.</i>

54
00:04:51,725 --> 00:04:55,962
<i>Has the Universe given me the right time</i>

55
00:04:55,962 --> 00:04:58,264
<i>to introduce myself to her?</i>

56
00:04:59,799 --> 00:05:04,570
<i>Is this the beginning of
my happily ever after?</i>

57
00:05:09,456 --> 00:05:12,102
Those who are getting off, be ready.

58
00:05:12,102 --> 00:05:14,537
We'll be at the bus stop in a few minutes.

59
00:05:24,445 --> 00:05:25,779
This is the stop!

60
00:05:25,779 --> 00:05:27,714
Time to wake up!

61
00:05:27,714 --> 00:05:29,648
Wake up!

62
00:05:38,098 --> 00:05:40,360
This is your stop.

63
00:05:40,360 --> 00:05:41,695
We've reached Huseña!

64
00:05:41,695 --> 00:05:43,763
Hurry up!

65
00:05:49,135 --> 00:05:56,009
Is it true that like a rosary,
love is full of mystery?

66
00:05:56,009 --> 00:05:59,846
Love isn't so mysterious, son.

67
00:05:59,846 --> 00:06:02,882
People just make it complicated sometimes.

68
00:06:02,882 --> 00:06:06,052
For me, love is very simple.

69
00:06:06,052 --> 00:06:10,793
Love is an act of bravery.

70
00:06:10,793 --> 00:06:17,608
You need to be brave
when opening your heart to others.

71
00:06:36,016 --> 00:06:39,785
<i>Love is an act of bravery.</i>

72
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:42,655
Has everyone gotten off?

73
00:07:00,741 --> 00:07:02,108
Hey...

74
00:07:02,108 --> 00:07:03,643
Sorry, I wasn't looking.

75
00:07:03,643 --> 00:07:05,044
I'm sorry.

76
00:07:14,067 --> 00:07:16,567
[Restroom]

77
00:07:23,706 --> 00:07:25,699
Ouch! Ouch!

78
00:07:25,699 --> 00:07:27,767
- What? Here! Get this! Who are you?
- That hurts!

79
00:07:27,767 --> 00:07:29,089
You've been following me!

80
00:07:29,089 --> 00:07:30,890
You think I wouldn't notice?

81
00:07:30,890 --> 00:07:32,425
- Pervert! Pervert!
- What do you mean?

82
00:07:32,425 --> 00:07:33,907
I'm not a pervert!

83
00:07:33,907 --> 00:07:36,663
- You're a robber!
- Come on, Joyce!

84
00:07:36,663 --> 00:07:38,123
I'm Liam!

85
00:07:38,123 --> 00:07:39,513
That hurts!

86
00:07:39,513 --> 00:07:41,901
How do you know my name?

87
00:07:41,901 --> 00:07:42,736
Are you a stalker?

88
00:07:42,736 --> 00:07:44,004
- No...
- A rapist and a stalker.

89
00:07:44,004 --> 00:07:45,152
- Robber!
- I'm not...

90
00:07:45,152 --> 00:07:46,239
A rapist who's also a stalker!

91
00:07:46,239 --> 00:07:48,742
Joyce! Joyce, calm down!

92
00:07:48,742 --> 00:07:51,244
I'm Liam. We were classmates in Agustin!

93
00:07:51,244 --> 00:07:52,730
It stings.

94
00:07:53,694 --> 00:07:56,516
You were my classmate in Agustin?

95
00:07:56,516 --> 00:08:02,488
Yes, we were classmates in Philosophy 101
under Professor Malvarosa.

96
00:08:03,390 --> 00:08:05,091
It hurts.

97
00:08:06,293 --> 00:08:09,062
We were classmates?

98
00:08:09,062 --> 00:08:11,097
- Yes.
- Are you sure?

99
00:08:11,097 --> 00:08:14,033
Yes, I am. We were classmates.

100
00:08:15,197 --> 00:08:17,470
What did you say your name was?

101
00:08:17,470 --> 00:08:18,968
Liam.

102
00:08:21,308 --> 00:08:23,401
Liam?

103
00:08:23,401 --> 00:08:25,317
William Herrera.

104
00:08:37,857 --> 00:08:38,858
Go on.

105
00:08:38,858 --> 00:08:41,200
- Do I just pour it?
- Yes.

106
00:08:42,076 --> 00:08:43,463
Sorry!

107
00:08:43,463 --> 00:08:46,012
I'm sorry. I'm really sorry.

108
00:08:46,012 --> 00:08:48,615
Sorry. Well, it was your fault.

109
00:08:48,615 --> 00:08:52,352
Why were you following me?

110
00:08:52,352 --> 00:08:54,687
Honestly, you can't blame me.

111
00:08:54,687 --> 00:08:59,778
You know how dangerous this world is
for women.

112
00:09:00,593 --> 00:09:04,931
Innocent women get killed.

113
00:09:04,931 --> 00:09:08,368
It's so unsafe nowadays. I'm sorry.

114
00:09:08,368 --> 00:09:09,502
Sorry.

115
00:09:09,502 --> 00:09:11,771
That's okay, Joyce.

116
00:09:11,771 --> 00:09:13,239
You're right.

117
00:09:13,239 --> 00:09:16,709
I should apologize because I startled you.

118
00:09:16,709 --> 00:09:19,044
But I didn't mean it.

119
00:09:20,471 --> 00:09:21,872
It's okay.

120
00:09:23,082 --> 00:09:24,717
So...

121
00:09:25,652 --> 00:09:29,855
What lesson did you learn today?

122
00:09:32,225 --> 00:09:35,762
What lesson did I learn today?

123
00:09:35,762 --> 00:09:41,901
Pepper spray hurts.

124
00:09:41,901 --> 00:09:43,736
Also...

125
00:09:43,736 --> 00:09:47,707
That pepper spray can be used
any time of the day.

126
00:09:47,707 --> 00:09:49,409
Also...

127
00:09:49,409 --> 00:09:54,614
I shouldn't just follow anyone
without being careful.

128
00:09:54,614 --> 00:09:58,585
You can be mistaken for a crook.
Look at what I've done to you.

129
00:09:58,585 --> 00:10:00,452
Sorry.

130
00:10:02,188 --> 00:10:05,725
Wait, so why were you following me?

131
00:10:05,725 --> 00:10:07,137
Do you need...

132
00:10:08,127 --> 00:10:11,297
Did I owe you money I haven't paid yet?

133
00:10:11,297 --> 00:10:12,799
Sorry! Sorry!

134
00:10:12,799 --> 00:10:13,766
- This is embarrassing!
- Joyce, Joyce...

135
00:10:13,766 --> 00:10:14,801
Sorry!

136
00:10:14,801 --> 00:10:17,637
You don't owe me anything.

137
00:10:17,637 --> 00:10:19,305
Nothing.

138
00:10:20,073 --> 00:10:24,143
I followed you, because...

139
00:10:26,930 --> 00:10:29,398
I wanted to...

140
00:10:31,340 --> 00:10:34,988
<i>At that moment, I wanted to confess to her.</i>

141
00:10:34,988 --> 00:10:38,525
<i>The truth is, I followed her</i>

142
00:10:38,525 --> 00:10:41,461
<i>because I wanted to introduce myself to her.</i>

143
00:10:41,461 --> 00:10:44,395
<i>I was hoping I could ask her out
to have coffee with me.</i>

144
00:10:44,395 --> 00:10:47,734
<i>Or maybe see a movie.</i>

145
00:10:47,734 --> 00:10:52,538
<i>But just like before,
I didn't have enough courage.</i>

146
00:11:01,247 --> 00:11:05,451
- Cheers to our professor!
- Cheers!

147
00:11:06,618 --> 00:11:08,621
Cheers!

148
00:11:08,621 --> 00:11:11,600
<i>Instead, I told her</i>

149
00:11:11,601 --> 00:11:16,763
<i>that Malvarosa, our philosophy professor,
will be having a send-off party.</i>

150
00:11:16,763 --> 00:11:19,666
<i>She and her husband would be migrating
to France,</i>

151
00:11:19,666 --> 00:11:22,166
<i>and she is inviting all of her students.</i>

152
00:11:22,167 --> 00:11:25,472
<i>And that's the reason why I followed her.</i>

153
00:11:25,472 --> 00:11:29,073
<i>To tell her
that I thought she might want to attend.</i>

154
00:11:29,073 --> 00:11:33,746
<i>She was one of our professor's favorites,
after all.</i>

155
00:11:35,408 --> 00:11:37,066
That's what I was saying...

156
00:11:37,066 --> 00:11:38,608
Let's take a picture!

157
00:11:38,608 --> 00:11:41,459
Everyone. One, two, smile.

158
00:11:59,472 --> 00:12:01,863
Maybe he's looking
for a girl he can dance with.

159
00:12:01,863 --> 00:12:03,876
- We have to find a girl.
- Oh, you!

160
00:12:03,876 --> 00:12:05,378
Come on, let's eat.

161
00:12:05,378 --> 00:12:06,646
- Oh, yeah.
- Let's go.

162
00:12:06,646 --> 00:12:08,514
- Ma'am.
- Go get some food.

163
00:12:34,207 --> 00:12:36,575
Are you waiting for...

164
00:12:37,977 --> 00:12:40,779
a shooting star so you can make a wish?

165
00:12:47,353 --> 00:12:51,857
Am I not too old to make wishes upon a star?

166
00:12:58,197 --> 00:13:00,432
You're right.

167
00:13:03,169 --> 00:13:06,538
I am also a believer of...

168
00:13:07,206 --> 00:13:09,041
hard work.

169
00:13:11,678 --> 00:13:16,482
I work hard to get the things I wish for.

170
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:23,789
I believe that...

171
00:13:24,948 --> 00:13:27,335
someday...

172
00:13:29,747 --> 00:13:32,740
all your wishes will come true.

173
00:13:36,582 --> 00:13:38,102
I hope so.

174
00:14:08,101 --> 00:14:09,932
You might be feeling cold.

175
00:14:13,673 --> 00:14:15,440
Thank you.

176
00:14:21,881 --> 00:14:27,452
So what does William Herrera do?

177
00:14:31,557 --> 00:14:33,159
How are you?

178
00:14:33,159 --> 00:14:36,361
How's life after college?

179
00:14:38,531 --> 00:14:45,170
I just started as a management trainee
in my dad's construction company.

180
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:50,376
Rich kid.

181
00:14:50,376 --> 00:14:51,954
Rich kid my foot.

182
00:14:51,954 --> 00:14:53,279
I'm not.

183
00:14:53,279 --> 00:14:54,580
- Yes, you are.
- No.

184
00:14:54,580 --> 00:14:55,882
Yes.

185
00:14:55,882 --> 00:14:59,318
But I'm hoping that after six months,

186
00:14:59,318 --> 00:15:02,655
I'll be promoted to project manager.

187
00:15:02,655 --> 00:15:07,492
Assuming that I won't disappoint my father.

188
00:15:09,195 --> 00:15:11,630
Are you not excited?

189
00:15:13,633 --> 00:15:19,905
Do you honestly think
that I dream of working for my dad?

190
00:15:22,875 --> 00:15:25,911
Well, right.

191
00:15:30,516 --> 00:15:32,050
Okay.

192
00:15:33,653 --> 00:15:36,133
If I were to choose,

193
00:15:36,133 --> 00:15:39,324
I would want to be...

194
00:15:40,493 --> 00:15:42,160
a writer.

195
00:15:45,665 --> 00:15:46,833
A writer?

196
00:15:46,833 --> 00:15:49,135
- See?
- For real?

197
00:15:49,135 --> 00:15:50,503
A writer?

198
00:15:50,503 --> 00:15:51,852
Yeah.

199
00:15:52,672 --> 00:15:55,876
Is that so unbelievable?

200
00:15:55,876 --> 00:15:57,343
I am sorry.

201
00:15:57,343 --> 00:16:01,113
That's not what I meant, but...

202
00:16:01,113 --> 00:16:02,148
A writer?

203
00:16:02,148 --> 00:16:04,049
- Yeah.
- I didn't...

204
00:16:04,684 --> 00:16:08,056
I didn't expect
that you'd dream of becoming a writer.

205
00:16:08,056 --> 00:16:13,326
It's not common
to meet someone who wants to be a writer.

206
00:16:13,326 --> 00:16:16,896
Are you saying that it's a worthless dream?

207
00:16:16,896 --> 00:16:19,365
It's not like that.

208
00:16:19,365 --> 00:16:21,067
Okay.

209
00:16:21,067 --> 00:16:25,016
Actually, I'm impressed.

210
00:16:25,016 --> 00:16:28,485
Very impressed, in fact.

211
00:16:29,442 --> 00:16:30,676
How about you?

212
00:16:30,676 --> 00:16:35,095
How is Miss Joycelyn Trinidad?

213
00:16:42,154 --> 00:16:43,855
Surviving.

214
00:16:44,631 --> 00:16:46,059
Okay.

215
00:16:48,318 --> 00:16:54,066
Yes, struggling. But it's manageable.

216
00:16:54,934 --> 00:16:57,036
I do modeling sometimes.

217
00:16:57,036 --> 00:16:59,071
Sometimes a promo girl.

218
00:16:59,071 --> 00:17:05,278
Sometimes an extra on TV or in film.

219
00:17:05,278 --> 00:17:09,915
Actually, I saw you in Lolong.

220
00:17:11,083 --> 00:17:13,319
- You did?
- Yes.

221
00:17:13,319 --> 00:17:15,090
I'm embarrassed, but how was it?

222
00:17:15,090 --> 00:17:17,991
Was I effective in my role?

223
00:17:17,991 --> 00:17:19,839
Well...

224
00:17:20,806 --> 00:17:23,911
Honestly, if there's an award

225
00:17:23,911 --> 00:17:29,235
for the most charming person
getting eaten by a crocodile...

226
00:17:29,235 --> 00:17:32,637
I guess, you will get it.

227
00:17:36,475 --> 00:17:39,467
I don't know
if I should be flattered or annoyed,

228
00:17:39,467 --> 00:17:42,221
but thank you.

229
00:17:44,850 --> 00:17:46,585
You know what?

230
00:17:50,256 --> 00:17:53,925
Life hasn't been easy for me.

231
00:18:00,626 --> 00:18:02,929
But I don't...

232
00:18:04,070 --> 00:18:06,491
I don't have regrets.

233
00:18:08,307 --> 00:18:11,676
I don't want to change anything because...

234
00:18:12,878 --> 00:18:15,981
Humans like us...

235
00:18:18,384 --> 00:18:21,520
We become better every day.

236
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:26,324
No matter
if we make the right or wrong decisions.

237
00:18:31,464 --> 00:18:33,332
You know what?

238
00:18:33,332 --> 00:18:36,635
I wish I am more like you, Miss Joyce.

239
00:18:37,937 --> 00:18:40,639
Because I have lots of regrets.

240
00:18:44,354 --> 00:18:45,923
Like what?

241
00:18:51,085 --> 00:18:53,253
Like...

242
00:18:56,390 --> 00:19:02,503
I wasn't able to tell the person I liked
how I truly felt.

243
00:19:12,220 --> 00:19:14,955
Why don't you tell her?

244
00:19:18,344 --> 00:19:21,313
You might regret it if you don't.

245
00:19:23,093 --> 00:19:27,063
What if she doesn't like me?

246
00:19:33,715 --> 00:19:36,083
What if she does?

247
00:19:38,945 --> 00:19:40,679
What if...

248
00:19:42,735 --> 00:19:46,627
she's now ready to open her heart to you?

249
00:19:47,640 --> 00:19:50,256
If you were in my place...

250
00:19:50,256 --> 00:19:52,544
what do you think I should do?

251
00:19:53,397 --> 00:19:58,501
Take a leap of faith, Mr. Herrera.

252
00:20:02,268 --> 00:20:05,270
Maybe she's just waiting for you.

253
00:20:06,972 --> 00:20:09,884
<i>Love isn't so mysterious.</i>

254
00:20:09,884 --> 00:20:12,678
<i>People just make it complicated sometimes.</i>

255
00:20:12,678 --> 00:20:16,649
<i>For me, love is very simple.</i>

256
00:20:16,649 --> 00:20:20,719
<i>Love is an act of bravery.</i>

257
00:20:20,719 --> 00:20:27,866
<i>You need to be brave
when you open up your heart to others.</i>

258
00:20:50,332 --> 00:20:52,213
Will you marry me?

259
00:20:54,248 --> 00:20:56,482
- Yes, yes.
- Yes?

260
00:21:02,027 --> 00:21:04,499
- Yes.
- Yes!

261
00:22:51,136 --> 00:22:52,738
Yes!

262
00:22:52,738 --> 00:22:54,672
Thank you!

263
00:23:18,677 --> 00:23:20,112
The baby moved!

264
00:23:20,112 --> 00:23:21,780
He kicked!

265
00:23:21,780 --> 00:23:22,815
There!

266
00:23:22,815 --> 00:23:25,150
Don't you hear it?

267
00:23:27,586 --> 00:23:28,821
- No.
- Why?

268
00:23:28,821 --> 00:23:30,356
Hey, hey.

269
00:23:30,356 --> 00:23:32,024
Why?

270
00:23:32,024 --> 00:23:34,780
Ma'am, we can already see the baby.
Count to three, okay?

271
00:23:34,780 --> 00:23:39,598
<i>Like I said, our story is like no other.</i>

272
00:23:39,598 --> 00:23:44,837
This story is not about
our "happily ever after".

273
00:23:44,837 --> 00:23:50,149
<i>It's about what happens
after "happily ever after".</i>

274
00:23:50,149 --> 00:23:53,120
One, two, three.

275
00:24:00,286 --> 00:24:02,554
Hey, when will you wake up?

276
00:24:02,554 --> 00:24:05,482
It's late! Your son will be late for school.

277
00:24:06,333 --> 00:24:09,328
Must I wake you up every time?
Can't you wake up on your own?

278
00:24:09,328 --> 00:24:11,230
Yes. Yes, hon.

279
00:24:11,230 --> 00:24:14,533
I'm going to get up, so please, relax.

280
00:24:14,533 --> 00:24:17,502
It's too early to get cranky.

281
00:24:20,706 --> 00:24:23,108
Why won't I get cranky?

282
00:24:23,108 --> 00:24:27,278
I have an important meeting.
Look at the time, Liam!

283
00:24:35,988 --> 00:24:37,764
It's already late to leave the house.

284
00:24:37,764 --> 00:24:39,024
It's already rush hour.
We will be stuck in traffic.

285
00:24:39,024 --> 00:24:41,160
Your son is going to be late. So wake up!

286
00:24:41,160 --> 00:24:44,829
Yes, yes. I'm already getting up.

287
00:24:45,931 --> 00:24:49,117
Get up or you will get it from me
if I am late.

288
00:25:14,259 --> 00:25:17,129
I told you we should hit the road by 5:30 AM.

289
00:25:17,129 --> 00:25:19,898
We would be late if we left at 6 AM.

290
00:25:19,898 --> 00:25:22,835
The traffic is already heavy.

291
00:25:22,835 --> 00:25:25,470
Your son will be late again.

292
00:25:29,608 --> 00:25:35,046
I told you I have a meeting
with an important client.

293
00:25:38,751 --> 00:25:41,819
You're compromising even my work.

294
00:25:46,424 --> 00:25:47,824
Hon...

295
00:25:48,704 --> 00:25:50,272
I'm sorry.

296
00:25:51,397 --> 00:25:56,262
I stayed up late revising my presentation.

297
00:25:56,262 --> 00:25:59,837
It's because you procrastinated.

298
00:26:03,108 --> 00:26:05,999
Talk to Dex's class adviser.

299
00:26:06,844 --> 00:26:08,781
She said your son can't afford
to be late anymore.

300
00:26:08,781 --> 00:26:11,883
He has been late many times
in this grading period.

301
00:26:16,688 --> 00:26:18,257
Talk to her and explain.

302
00:26:18,257 --> 00:26:21,693
Tell her it's your fault
that your son is late.

303
00:26:28,600 --> 00:26:30,033
- Hey, what are you doing?
- Hey!

304
00:26:30,033 --> 00:26:31,514
You cut us off!

305
00:26:38,010 --> 00:26:39,812
We're almost at Dex's school.

306
00:26:39,812 --> 00:26:41,692
We can get there faster if we run.

307
00:26:41,692 --> 00:26:43,314
Give me your bag.

308
00:26:44,216 --> 00:26:45,883
- Is this all you need?
- What about me?

309
00:26:46,852 --> 00:26:51,365
Hon, can you book a motorcycle
so you can get to work faster?

310
00:27:01,133 --> 00:27:05,189
Sweetie, be safe, okay?

311
00:27:05,189 --> 00:27:07,673
Mommy's going to work now.

312
00:27:07,673 --> 00:27:10,242
Make sure you eat.
Mommy made you a yummy meal.

313
00:27:10,242 --> 00:27:13,178
It's your favorite.
Make sure to eat it, okay?

314
00:27:13,178 --> 00:27:14,179
I love you.

315
00:27:14,179 --> 00:27:15,852
Love you.

316
00:27:19,451 --> 00:27:22,921
We'll talk later. We can't stay like this.

317
00:27:22,921 --> 00:27:25,290
See you later, Mommy.

318
00:27:30,963 --> 00:27:33,098
Oh no, Daddy.

319
00:27:33,098 --> 00:27:36,435
Mommy is mad at you again.

320
00:27:36,435 --> 00:27:38,837
Sweetie, Mom's not mad.

321
00:27:38,837 --> 00:27:44,631
That's how your mom shows her love.
Straight to the point.

322
00:27:46,078 --> 00:27:48,447
So, are you ready?

323
00:27:48,447 --> 00:27:49,881
Come on.

324
00:28:02,552 --> 00:28:03,852
Let's go.

325
00:28:09,368 --> 00:28:11,069
Let's go?

326
00:28:15,607 --> 00:28:21,313
<i>Who said stories should end
in happily ever after?</i>

327
00:28:21,313 --> 00:28:22,814
<i>Don't worry.</i>

328
00:28:22,814 --> 00:28:25,416
<i>This is not one of those stories.</i>

329
00:28:29,922 --> 00:28:35,160
<i>Who said stories should end
in happily ever after?</i>

330
00:28:35,160 --> 00:28:36,595
<i>Don't worry.</i>

331
00:28:36,595 --> 00:28:39,430
<i>This is not one of those stories.</i>

332
00:28:40,566 --> 00:28:45,169
<i>Like in a movie, this is just a trailer.</i>

333
00:28:49,007 --> 00:28:50,542
Hello, Dex.

334
00:28:50,542 --> 00:28:55,547
<i>Because what happens
after "happily ever after" is more realistic.</i>

335
00:28:55,547 --> 00:29:00,018
<i>It tells a more realistic story of love.</i>

336
00:29:31,303 --> 00:29:33,233
People say

337
00:29:33,234 --> 00:29:38,477
that love is the most powerful force
in the universe.

338
00:29:38,477 --> 00:29:43,622
Others say that love is destiny.

339
00:29:43,622 --> 00:29:46,591
Love is kind.

340
00:29:47,459 --> 00:29:49,427
But for me...

341
00:29:50,629 --> 00:29:55,500
Love is an act of bravery.

342
00:29:55,500 --> 00:30:02,073
Brave enough to open your heart
to less-than-ideal situations.

343
00:30:02,073 --> 00:30:05,443
Brave enough to face the challenges

344
00:30:05,443 --> 00:30:09,648
that time and fate throw at you.

345
00:30:09,648 --> 00:30:14,786
Brave enough to put in the hard work
to make it work.

346
00:30:14,786 --> 00:30:18,190
And this story is about that kind of love.

347
00:30:18,190 --> 00:30:23,327
The truest kind of love.

348
00:30:37,642 --> 00:30:39,711
Hi, son.

349
00:30:39,711 --> 00:30:42,514
Mommy, I have a new tablet.

350
00:30:42,514 --> 00:30:47,018
Daddy gave it to me because I am a good boy.

351
00:30:54,446 --> 00:30:56,114
Where's your daddy?

352
00:30:56,114 --> 00:30:57,883
Over there. Making dinner.

353
00:30:57,883 --> 00:31:00,652
Hon, you're home.

354
00:31:00,652 --> 00:31:03,721
Come on,
let's eat while the food is still hot.

355
00:31:07,186 --> 00:31:13,547
Did I forget something
that we should celebrate?

356
00:31:14,900 --> 00:31:16,134
You did.

357
00:31:16,134 --> 00:31:19,203
And we should really celebrate this, hon.

358
00:31:22,841 --> 00:31:25,910
So it's true that you gave Dex a gift?

359
00:31:27,913 --> 00:31:29,514
Come on.

360
00:31:29,514 --> 00:31:31,483
Don't be jealous.

361
00:31:31,483 --> 00:31:33,318
Do you think it's just Dex?

362
00:31:33,318 --> 00:31:35,953
I also got you something.

363
00:31:42,027 --> 00:31:44,662
Go on. Open it, my love.

364
00:31:46,968 --> 00:31:52,767
[Air Filipinas]
[To: Paris, France]

365
00:32:05,909 --> 00:32:07,806
What is this for?

366
00:32:08,687 --> 00:32:10,522
For us.

367
00:32:10,522 --> 00:32:16,862
Maybe it's about time
we fulfill our dream vacation in Paris.

368
00:32:16,862 --> 00:32:18,663
So there.

369
00:32:22,281 --> 00:32:24,583
Can we talk?

370
00:32:32,344 --> 00:32:34,212
What do you think are you doing?

371
00:32:34,212 --> 00:32:36,722
Where did you get the money for this?

372
00:32:37,515 --> 00:32:39,817
I used my credit card.

373
00:32:41,353 --> 00:32:45,122
So you also bought Dex's tablet on credit?

374
00:32:46,191 --> 00:32:48,393
Hon, just relax.

375
00:32:48,393 --> 00:32:50,695
Let me explain.

376
00:32:52,230 --> 00:32:55,600
Liam, what is there to explain?

377
00:32:55,600 --> 00:32:57,736
You know that we only earn enough.

378
00:32:57,736 --> 00:33:01,773
Barely enough for Dex's schooling.

379
00:33:01,773 --> 00:33:04,576
And now, this?

380
00:33:04,576 --> 00:33:06,945
Are you using your head?

381
00:33:06,945 --> 00:33:09,414
Hon, come on. It's okay.

382
00:33:09,414 --> 00:33:15,420
My new show got approved.
That means we have extra income.

383
00:33:15,420 --> 00:33:18,890
So you think you have money
just because you have a new show?

384
00:33:18,890 --> 00:33:20,991
Like you hit the jackpot?

385
00:33:23,128 --> 00:33:25,730
Are we one-day millionaires?

386
00:33:26,641 --> 00:33:29,301
Liam, we should save when we have extra money

387
00:33:29,301 --> 00:33:32,069
instead of compulsively spending!

388
00:33:34,639 --> 00:33:37,527
What if we have an emergency?

389
00:33:37,527 --> 00:33:40,854
What will happen to Dex?
Where will you get the money?

390
00:33:43,090 --> 00:33:47,132
Hon, I just thought

391
00:33:47,133 --> 00:33:52,732
that maybe we need a break
from stress, you know?

392
00:33:55,260 --> 00:33:57,228
You thought of it?

393
00:33:58,163 --> 00:34:00,765
Did you really think it through?

394
00:34:01,666 --> 00:34:04,368
Liam, are you really using your head?

395
00:34:05,021 --> 00:34:06,545
Huh?

396
00:34:07,512 --> 00:34:08,834
Because if you are,

397
00:34:08,834 --> 00:34:12,644
you should have realized
that we don't need this.

398
00:34:12,644 --> 00:34:13,945
If you only use your head,

399
00:34:13,945 --> 00:34:15,981
you will realize
that we can't afford to go on vacation,

400
00:34:15,981 --> 00:34:19,483
because we will starve after!

401
00:34:23,822 --> 00:34:27,292
<i>Son, love isn't so mysterious.</i>

402
00:34:27,292 --> 00:34:31,129
For me, love is very simple.

403
00:34:31,129 --> 00:34:36,801
Because love is an act of bravery.

404
00:34:36,801 --> 00:34:44,575
You need to be brave
to open your heart to others.

405
00:34:47,112 --> 00:34:48,846
I'm sorry.

406
00:34:51,049 --> 00:34:54,570
Don't worry. I'll return everything tomorrow.

407
00:34:55,280 --> 00:34:59,283
I'll ask for a refund for everything I spent.

408
00:35:27,120 --> 00:35:28,543
Gosh.

409
00:35:34,426 --> 00:35:35,795
Hon.

410
00:35:35,795 --> 00:35:37,563
Hon...

411
00:35:37,563 --> 00:35:40,231
I overslept.

412
00:35:40,231 --> 00:35:42,067
Hon, sorry. I overslept.

413
00:35:42,067 --> 00:35:44,235
My alarm didn't work.

414
00:35:44,235 --> 00:35:47,337
I know. I turned off your alarm.

415
00:35:48,204 --> 00:35:53,378
Looks like you stayed up all night,
so I didn't wake you up.

416
00:35:53,378 --> 00:35:55,213
What?

417
00:35:55,213 --> 00:35:57,074
What about Dex?

418
00:35:58,616 --> 00:36:01,352
Our car was towed, remember?

419
00:36:01,352 --> 00:36:03,221
I called my mom.

420
00:36:03,221 --> 00:36:07,224
I asked her to bring Dex to school for now.

421
00:36:13,765 --> 00:36:15,934
By the way...

422
00:36:15,934 --> 00:36:18,770
Your dad called.

423
00:36:18,770 --> 00:36:23,668
He was cleaning and saw these things
that belonged to your mom.

424
00:36:23,668 --> 00:36:25,995
Why did he bring it only now?

425
00:36:25,995 --> 00:36:28,497
Good thing his new wife didn't get rid of it.

426
00:36:32,717 --> 00:36:37,221
There are photo albums here
that we can show to Dex.

427
00:36:41,126 --> 00:36:43,795
I miss your mom.

428
00:36:43,795 --> 00:36:46,430
I miss her cooking.

429
00:36:48,466 --> 00:36:51,101
We can show these to Dex.

430
00:36:54,606 --> 00:36:56,874
What else is there, hon?

431
00:37:01,679 --> 00:37:02,947
Well... what is this...

432
00:37:02,947 --> 00:37:04,315
What is it?

433
00:37:04,315 --> 00:37:08,039
- Is it heavy?
- What is this?

434
00:37:08,039 --> 00:37:09,840
I wonder what it is.

435
00:37:11,489 --> 00:37:13,291
- I think you open it here.
- This side?

436
00:37:13,291 --> 00:37:14,733
There.

437
00:37:22,967 --> 00:37:24,769
I didn't know
that mom also had something like this.

438
00:37:24,769 --> 00:37:26,937
Was she a writer, too?

439
00:37:27,882 --> 00:37:29,716
I don't know.

440
00:37:32,977 --> 00:37:36,314
I'll put away Mom's things.

441
00:37:36,314 --> 00:37:39,103
Let me do it, hon.
I'll bring it to the storage room.

442
00:37:39,103 --> 00:37:40,904
I got it.

443
00:37:43,979 --> 00:37:45,584
Hon...

444
00:37:55,533 --> 00:37:58,268
I'm sorry for last night.

445
00:38:01,372 --> 00:38:03,140
It's okay.

446
00:38:04,909 --> 00:38:06,944
You were right.

447
00:38:13,718 --> 00:38:15,652
Actually...

448
00:38:17,722 --> 00:38:19,690
I was wrong.

449
00:38:27,405 --> 00:38:30,741
I was wrong because I overreacted.

450
00:38:31,896 --> 00:38:34,031
I know...

451
00:38:38,919 --> 00:38:42,647
that you're just trying
to be a good father...

452
00:38:44,478 --> 00:38:46,023
and a good husband.

453
00:38:51,999 --> 00:38:58,762
I'm sorry because instead of being happy...

454
00:39:00,471 --> 00:39:03,307
instead of thanking you...

455
00:39:06,771 --> 00:39:09,039
I judged you.

456
00:39:11,523 --> 00:39:16,260
I said some hurtful words.

457
00:39:18,216 --> 00:39:20,918
I should be the one to apologize.

458
00:39:21,653 --> 00:39:23,587
I should have been...

459
00:39:25,123 --> 00:39:28,725
I should have been
more mindful in my decisions.

460
00:39:30,795 --> 00:39:33,797
I shouldn't make decisions on my own.

461
00:39:36,240 --> 00:39:39,076
We can still go.

462
00:39:40,965 --> 00:39:43,266
We'll go to Paris?

463
00:39:44,008 --> 00:39:45,410
Don't you want to?

464
00:39:45,410 --> 00:39:47,444
Of course, I do.

465
00:39:48,146 --> 00:39:53,251
But you said we should not spend compulsively

466
00:39:53,251 --> 00:39:58,208
so when there's an emergency,
we have savings.

467
00:39:58,208 --> 00:40:00,129
Hon, you know what?

468
00:40:01,492 --> 00:40:06,897
I am about to close a deal
with a big account later.

469
00:40:08,927 --> 00:40:10,110
If I get that,

470
00:40:10,111 --> 00:40:13,601
I will provide insurance
for all the employees

471
00:40:13,601 --> 00:40:16,560
of a big-time businessman.

472
00:40:16,560 --> 00:40:20,171
Hon, I'm sure
I'll get a huge commission from it.

473
00:40:20,171 --> 00:40:22,180
Wow.

474
00:40:22,180 --> 00:40:24,782
Congratulations, hon.

475
00:40:24,782 --> 00:40:28,830
So that means
our Parisian honeymoon is really on.

476
00:40:29,654 --> 00:40:31,456
Dex will soon have a sibling.

477
00:40:31,456 --> 00:40:32,457
Silly.

478
00:40:32,457 --> 00:40:34,324
Why not?

479
00:40:43,039 --> 00:40:44,840
I love you.

480
00:40:46,804 --> 00:40:49,506
I love you, too. So much.

481
00:40:52,910 --> 00:40:54,711
So much.

482
00:41:06,891 --> 00:41:09,227
<i>After all the stories I told you,</i>

483
00:41:09,227 --> 00:41:12,044
<i>I'm sure you still have some questions left.</i>

484
00:41:12,044 --> 00:41:14,479
<i>What could possibly go wrong?</i>

485
00:41:16,868 --> 00:41:18,503
What?

486
00:41:18,503 --> 00:41:20,338
Are you kidding?

487
00:41:20,338 --> 00:41:23,741
I developed that story for almost a year.

488
00:41:23,741 --> 00:41:25,576
Look, Liam.

489
00:41:25,576 --> 00:41:28,940
I am sorry to be the bearer of bad news.

490
00:41:28,940 --> 00:41:33,251
But the network has decided
not to proceed with your concept.

491
00:41:33,251 --> 00:41:36,520
And that decision has already been made.

492
00:41:44,429 --> 00:41:46,364
Sir, you can't do this to me.

493
00:41:46,364 --> 00:41:48,099
I need this story.

494
00:41:48,099 --> 00:41:49,634
I need this project.

495
00:41:49,634 --> 00:41:52,226
You said you think the story was good,

496
00:41:52,226 --> 00:41:56,040
and it was very promising
when it comes to viewer engagement.

497
00:41:56,040 --> 00:41:58,376
Liam, relax.

498
00:41:58,376 --> 00:41:59,444
Relax?

499
00:41:59,444 --> 00:42:00,778
Sir, how can I relax?

500
00:42:00,778 --> 00:42:03,448
The concept that I've long been working on
is gone!

501
00:42:03,448 --> 00:42:06,317
You have to understand, Liam.

502
00:42:06,317 --> 00:42:09,253
Television is still very traditional.

503
00:42:09,253 --> 00:42:12,557
Your concept is too high.

504
00:42:12,557 --> 00:42:14,292
It's too modern.

505
00:42:14,292 --> 00:42:16,793
Our audience can't relate to it.

506
00:42:16,793 --> 00:42:17,962
So, what now?

507
00:42:17,962 --> 00:42:20,565
- Do I just give it up?
- I didn't say that.

508
00:42:20,565 --> 00:42:22,092
What I'm saying is

509
00:42:22,092 --> 00:42:26,829
there are still other platforms
we can explore.

510
00:42:29,891 --> 00:42:32,092
What do you mean?

511
00:42:40,985 --> 00:42:42,487
What I'm saying is

512
00:42:42,487 --> 00:42:47,325
there is opportunity for it
in the streaming platforms.

513
00:42:47,325 --> 00:42:48,993
Well, generally speaking,

514
00:42:48,993 --> 00:42:52,630
your story is more suitable
for the digital audience.

515
00:42:52,630 --> 00:42:56,928
The highly educated ones
with disposable income.

516
00:42:56,928 --> 00:43:02,640
Young professionals
with unique viewing habits.

517
00:43:02,640 --> 00:43:05,321
So you mean there's still a chance
for my show to get produced?

518
00:43:05,321 --> 00:43:06,677
Of course!

519
00:43:06,677 --> 00:43:09,955
That's why I want to introduce you to Charry.

520
00:43:14,685 --> 00:43:16,521
Your timing is perfect, Liam.

521
00:43:16,521 --> 00:43:19,968
I am really looking for creators like you!

522
00:43:19,968 --> 00:43:20,764
See?

523
00:43:20,765 --> 00:43:23,861
And as they say,
actually, as Gen Z would say,

524
00:43:23,861 --> 00:43:28,226
content is king, and content is our future.

525
00:43:28,226 --> 00:43:29,167
Aren't you excited?

526
00:43:29,167 --> 00:43:31,369
Gosh, there's a lot I want to say,

527
00:43:31,369 --> 00:43:35,300
but I am sure that, you know,
your future is so bright.

528
00:43:35,300 --> 00:43:39,210
Assuming we don't destroy the planet,

529
00:43:39,210 --> 00:43:42,133
your future is really bright.

530
00:43:42,133 --> 00:43:45,136
Content creator, the best. Right?

531
00:43:45,136 --> 00:43:47,672
That's what I've been telling Liam.

532
00:43:47,672 --> 00:43:51,883
- He is one of the network's best writers.
- Wow!

533
00:43:51,883 --> 00:43:54,912
But I think television
is too small a pond for him.

534
00:43:54,912 --> 00:43:55,725
True.

535
00:43:55,725 --> 00:43:58,816
So I honestly believe
we have an opportunity here.

536
00:43:58,816 --> 00:44:02,487
Cha here is the head of DigiTV.

537
00:44:02,487 --> 00:44:06,567
One of the fastest-growing
online content platforms

538
00:44:06,567 --> 00:44:08,025
in the region.

539
00:44:08,025 --> 00:44:09,994
Wow!

540
00:44:09,994 --> 00:44:12,663
Ma'am, it's nice to meet you.

541
00:44:12,663 --> 00:44:19,504
It's an honor for me
to share my passion for storytelling.

542
00:44:19,504 --> 00:44:20,400
Great!

543
00:44:20,400 --> 00:44:24,420
So tell me,
what story do you want to tell?

544
00:44:34,792 --> 00:44:37,076
Oh, why?

545
00:44:37,077 --> 00:44:39,345
Do you have to go somewhere?

546
00:44:40,938 --> 00:44:43,294
N-No, I don't.

547
00:44:43,294 --> 00:44:44,695
I don't have other plans.

548
00:44:44,695 --> 00:44:45,696
It's okay.

549
00:44:45,696 --> 00:44:46,797
No problem.

550
00:44:46,797 --> 00:44:48,866
Okay. So, what are you waiting for?

551
00:44:48,866 --> 00:44:51,469
Pitch your great idea to me, and let's see.

552
00:44:51,469 --> 00:44:52,133
What is it?

553
00:44:52,133 --> 00:44:56,607
Is it a survival game
in a post-apocalyptic world?

554
00:45:03,123 --> 00:45:05,024
- Mom!
- Sweetie.

555
00:45:09,654 --> 00:45:11,455
Bye, Dex.

556
00:45:12,924 --> 00:45:14,691
Let's go.

557
00:45:29,407 --> 00:45:31,856
Dex, why are you still here?

558
00:45:31,856 --> 00:45:34,011
Who will pick you up today?

559
00:45:34,011 --> 00:45:35,246
My daddy.

560
00:45:35,246 --> 00:45:37,582
Maybe he's stuck in traffic.

561
00:45:37,582 --> 00:45:39,450
Okay, just wait here. Okay?

562
00:45:39,450 --> 00:45:41,852
I'll be inside.

563
00:45:51,062 --> 00:45:54,367
Our platinum health insurance
will provide your employees

564
00:45:54,367 --> 00:45:56,867
with comprehensive health benefits.

565
00:45:56,867 --> 00:45:58,816
Aside from hospitalization,

566
00:45:58,816 --> 00:46:02,965
we also provide coverage
if your employee needs long-term therapy,

567
00:46:02,965 --> 00:46:06,268
including mental health services.

568
00:46:07,545 --> 00:46:09,280
She used to be an actress, right?

569
00:46:09,280 --> 00:46:11,749
Her career did not go anywhere
after she got pregnant.

570
00:46:11,749 --> 00:46:14,418
Oh, what a waste.

571
00:46:14,418 --> 00:46:16,153
That's what she got for being a flirt.

572
00:46:16,153 --> 00:46:18,522
She made the wrong choices.

573
00:46:26,397 --> 00:46:28,966
The advantage of this, sir,

574
00:46:28,966 --> 00:46:32,466
is that if your employee gets sick...

575
00:46:32,467 --> 00:46:34,834
[Incoming Call]

576
00:46:38,683 --> 00:46:42,587
Our priority is to provide your employees...

577
00:46:42,587 --> 00:46:44,449
the best healthcare there is.

578
00:46:44,449 --> 00:46:48,849
We will nurse them back to health,
and make them productive again.

579
00:46:48,849 --> 00:46:52,521
But, sir, let me discuss
how much more you can save

580
00:46:52,521 --> 00:46:56,459
by availing our corporate package.

581
00:47:02,333 --> 00:47:05,368
Your mom's not answering her phone.

582
00:47:09,140 --> 00:47:11,684
Let's try calling your dad.

583
00:47:16,523 --> 00:47:19,150
He's also not picking up.

584
00:47:19,150 --> 00:47:22,653
Maybe they're already
on their way here, Teacher.

585
00:47:22,653 --> 00:47:25,455
I'll just wait for them.

586
00:47:26,157 --> 00:47:27,825
I'll go to the office first.

587
00:47:27,825 --> 00:47:29,493
I'll double-check from the file

588
00:47:29,493 --> 00:47:32,263
if I have the correct contact numbers
of your parents.

589
00:47:32,263 --> 00:47:34,768
Stay here, okay?

590
00:48:12,009 --> 00:48:13,091
Sir!

591
00:48:13,091 --> 00:48:14,510
- Sir!
- Boss, to City General.

592
00:48:14,510 --> 00:48:16,584
Sir, where are you going? Sir, wait!

593
00:48:16,584 --> 00:48:18,892
- Let's go.
- Sir!

594
00:48:18,892 --> 00:48:21,428
Don't party too much, sir.

595
00:48:21,428 --> 00:48:25,239
You can be forgetful
when you're having too much fun.

596
00:48:33,075 --> 00:48:35,078
Hey!

597
00:48:35,078 --> 00:48:36,328
Why are you hugging my wife?

598
00:48:36,328 --> 00:48:37,542
He's been acting weird, Ma'am.

599
00:48:37,542 --> 00:48:39,083
I'm worried about his situation right now.

600
00:48:39,083 --> 00:48:40,347
Wait, wait!

601
00:48:40,347 --> 00:48:42,305
Pervert!
